Summary: Diablo II: Resurrected: leave out the DXVK and DXMT DLL paths
Category: graphics
Kind: workaround
Origin: reconstructed
  Version: Sikarugir 10.0_8
  Binary: WS12WineSikarugir10.0_8 ntdll.so
  Functions: set_dll_path (inlined into init_paths, 0x1e4b3-0x1e760)
  Changes: none: the same rules as 10.0_8
  Note: Sikarugir-only: no CrossOver 26, wine-staging or WineHQ equivalent
Origin: wine-mac-builds
  Version: 10.0
  Changes: without the WINEDLLPATH_D3DMETAL row and SIKARUGIR_D2R_FORCE_VKD3D:
    a skip_for_d2r flag replaces the three-way rule
Upstream: no
Why: Diablo II: Resurrected (D2R.exe, matched by substring on argv[1]) never
 gets the WINEDLLPATH_DXVK or WINEDLLPATH_DXMT folders (unconditionally, as
 in 10.0_8), so it runs on Wine's own d3d12 (vkd3d) and dxgi instead.
 Sikarugir (and the 10.0 copy) also skips WINEDLLPATH_D3DMETAL for it when
 SIKARUGIR_D2R_FORCE_VKD3D is set; this copy doesn't search that path at all,
 so the variable has no effect here.
Programs: Diablo II: Resurrected (D2R.exe): presumably because it uses
 Direct3D 12, which DXVK and DXMT don't provide, while their dxgi.dll would
 replace the one Wine's d3d12 needs
Matches: exe D2R.exe
Enable: see ntdll-renderer-dll-paths (WINEDLLPATH_DXVK or WINEDLLPATH_DXMT set)
Uncertain: why Sikarugir does this: 10.0_8 doesn't record a reason (Programs
 gives the likely one).
Expects before it: ntdll-renderer-dll-paths, ntdll-launcher-metal-hud (context)
No test: none written yet; a D2R.exe copy of renderer-dll-paths' program under
 WINEDLLPATH_DXVK, which must get Wine's d3d11, would cover it
Status: 11.21, 11.22: 2026-11-26: WINEDLLPATH_D3DMETAL and
 SIKARUGIR_D2R_FORCE_VKD3D removed
 11.21: 2026-11-26: quick builds 20261126T005336 and T023339 (macOS 26.7.2,
 M1 Max): smoke and the regression suite passed
 11.22: 2026-11-26: quick builds 20261126T002454 and T025644 (macOS 26.7.2,
 M1 Max): smoke and the regression suite passed

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -329,6 +329,12 @@ static BOOL is_launcher_process(void)
     return FALSE;
 }
 
+/* Sikarugir: Diablo II: Resurrected runs on vkd3d rather than DXVK or DXMT */
+static BOOL is_d2r_process(void)
+{
+    return main_argc >= 2 && strstr( main_argv[1], "D2R.exe" );
+}
+
 /* Sikarugir: per-renderer DLL directories, searched before the builtin ones. Sikarugir
  * also has WINEDLLPATH_D3DMETAL, first: D3DMetal 3.0 needs Wine 10.4's GSBASE model,
  * so it is left out here. */
@@ -336,12 +342,13 @@ static const struct
 {
     const char *var;
     BOOL skip_for_launchers;
+    BOOL skip_for_d2r;
 } renderer_dll_paths[] =
 {
-    { "WINEDLLPATH_CNCD",     FALSE },
-    { "WINEDLLPATH_D9VK",     TRUE },
-    { "WINEDLLPATH_DXVK",     TRUE },
-    { "WINEDLLPATH_DXMT",     FALSE },
+    { "WINEDLLPATH_CNCD",     FALSE, FALSE },
+    { "WINEDLLPATH_D9VK",     TRUE,  FALSE },
+    { "WINEDLLPATH_DXVK",     TRUE,  TRUE },
+    { "WINEDLLPATH_DXMT",     FALSE, TRUE },
 };
 
 static BOOL use_renderer_dll_path( unsigned int idx )
@@ -359,6 +366,7 @@ static BOOL use_renderer_dll_path( unsigned int idx )
         }
         return FALSE;
     }
+    if (renderer_dll_paths[idx].skip_for_d2r && is_d2r_process()) return FALSE;
     return TRUE;
 }
 
